      "answer": "Alphabet's most recent 10-Q describes that additional issuances of its Class A stock or Class C stock under its ATM Program could dilute its existing stockholders or otherwise depress the market prices of its Class A stock and Class C stock. The ATM Program allows Alphabet to offer and sell up to $40 billion of shares of its Class A stock and Class C stock to or through sales agents under established limits. Any sales under the ATM Program could have dilutive effects for Alphabet's existing stockholders over time. The market prices of Alphabet's Class A stock or Class C stock is likely to be influenced by any sales under its ATM Program. The ATM Program could result in a depression in the market price of Alphabet's Class A stock or Class C stock due to dilution.",
